    "content": "Long Island University (LIU) is a private, NCAA Division I research university in New York (founded 1926) with campuses in Brooklyn and Brookville. It is recognized for high research activity and offers diverse programs, including the Roc Nation School. \"Liu\" is also a common Chinese surname, meaning harmony or beauty. Key Details About LIU (Long Island University): Campuses: Brookville (Post) and Brooklyn. Athletics: LIU Sharks, competing in NCAA Division I. Rankings: Top 7% of research universities nationwide. Academics: Offers a wide range of undergraduate and graduate degrees, featuring the Roc Nation School of Music, Sports & Entertainment. Admissions: Known to be lightly selective with an acceptance rate around 89-90%. Other \"Liu\" References: Alysa Liu: An American figure skater who won gold in 2026. Surname: One of the most common surnames in mainland China, often representing 5% or more of the population. Common Searches for LIU: LIU Portal/Login: Students often search for the MyLIU portal to access grades and schedules. LIU Brooklyn vs. Post: Information on the two distinct campuses. LIU Tuition: Tuition and fees are approximately $42,000+ annually.",
